                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 7 at 7:38PM HST until September 7 at 10:30PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "FFWHFO\n\nThe National Weather Service in Honolulu has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe island of Kauai in Kauai County\n\n* Until 1030 PM HST.\n\n* At 738 PM HST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain over Kauai. Rain\nwas falling at a rate of 1 to 2 inches per hour. Substantial rises\nhave been observed at the Wainiha River and Waialae Stream gages.\nRises on other area rivers and streams can also be expected as\nheavy rain continues. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to\nbegin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLihue, Kapaa, Kalaheo, Kekaha, Princeville, Kilauea, North Fork\nWailua Trails, Alakai Swamp Trails, Lawai, Omao, Kokee State Park\nand Wailua Homesteads.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
